[agent] ## Summary
[agent] Created training dataset **`churntrainingc8f821`, version 1** on Hopsworks via the Python SDK (SDK mode — all joins/transforms ran platform-side).
[agent] **Approach — point-in-time-correct join via the feature view:**
[agent] 1. Created 5 offline feature groups, each with `account_id` as primary key and `event_time` set: `..._transactions`, `..._profiles`, `..._activity`, `..._account_health`, and `..._labels` (event_time = `label_time`).
[agent] 2. Inserted `transactions.csv` **and** `transactions_late.csv` into the same transactions FG (same schema, same data).
[agent] 3. Built feature view `churntrainingc8f821` v1 with the **labels FG as the root** (its `label_time` is the reference timestamp). Each joined FG contributes its most recent value with `event_time ≤ label_time` — Hopsworks performs the PIT join automatically; rows with `event_time > label_time` are never used.
[agent] 4. Materialized training dataset version 1 (parquet) through the Feature Query Service.
[agent] **Verification (read back through the platform):**
[agent] - Exactly the 9 required columns: `account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score, churned`.
[agent] - 100 rows — one per row of `labels.csv`.
[agent] - Zero nulls.
[agent] - PIT spot-check on 8 random accounts confirmed `amount` and `credit_score` match the most-recent-at-or-before-`label_time` value computed from the raw CSVs (including the late transactions export).
